## Specialized Custom Agents
To invoke specialized agents in GitHub Copilot Chat, use `@<agent>`:
- `@orchestrator`: Governs lifecycle gate transitions (G0–G6) and validates contracts.
- `@discovery`: Conducts read-only inspection of repository structure and tools for Gate G0.
- `@design`: Specifies design tokens, responsive breakpoints, and WCAG accessibility for Gate G2.
- `@architecture`: Author systems architecture, data models, schemas, and ADRs for Gate G3.
- `@planning`: Generates phased Work Breakdown Structures (WBS) and file ownership matrices.
- `@implementation`: Authors production-grade code within strictly assigned file boundaries.
- `@verification`: Executes test suites, linters, and type checkers to collect execution telemetry.
- `@independent-review`: Adversarially audits diffs, anti-slop rules, and security posture for Gate G5.
- `@documentation-and-memory`: Reconciles 3-tier memory and prepares the Gate G6 Release Contract.

